         `salary row` 33 8344.82 7883.49 7357.82 7030.88 6409.16,
         `salary row` 34 8428.26 7962.32 7431.40 7101.20 6473.26,
         `salary row` 35 8512.55 8041.95 7505.72 7172.20 6537.99,
         `salary row` 36 8597.67 8122.36 7580.77 7243.93 6603.37

-- §1a: the table in force on a day (no table of this circular before 1.9.2017).
@ref akn:art_1__para_a
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A LIST OF `salary row`
DECIDE `the table in force on` `the day` IS
    IF `the day` AT LEAST Date 1 12 2018
    THEN `the combined-salary table from 1.12.2018`
    ELSE IF `the day` AT LEAST Date 1 9 2017
         THEN `the combined-salary table from 1.9.2017`
         ELSE EMPTY

-- §1b: the new tables move with the cost-of-living increments, at their
-- dates and rates, which are set elsewhere: an input here.
@ref akn:art_1__para_b
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      d IS A `teacher's degree`
      `seniority` IS A NUMBER
      `cost-of-living rate since the table` IS A NUMBER @desc the cost-of-living increments paid since the table's date, compounded, as a fraction; set elsewhere
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `combined salary` `the day` d `seniority` `cost-of-living rate since the table` IS
    sum (map (GIVEN r YIELD `the cell for` r d)
             (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `seniority year` EQUALS `seniority`) (`the table in force on` `the day`)))
    TIMES (1 PLUS `cost-of-living rate since the table`)

-- §1c: a percentage supplement that continues after the agreement is
-- computed on the new combined salary.
@ref akn:art_1__para_c
GIVEN `rate` IS A NUMBER, `the new combined salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a continuing percentage supplement` `rate` `the new combined salary` IS
    `rate` TIMES `the new combined salary`

§§ `2 הגדלת תוספת שקלית 2016`

@desc A period of the updated 2016 shekel supplement and its amount for a full position.
DECLARE `shekel period` HAS
    `period from`   IS A DATE
    `period to`     IS A DATE  @desc 31.12.9999 stands for "ואילך"
    `full-position amount` IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_2__para_a__subpara_1 akn:art_2__para_a__subpara_2 akn:art_2__para_a__subpara_3 akn:art_2__para_a__subpara_4
`the updated shekel supplement 2016` MEANS
    LIST `shekel period` (Date 1 9 2017)  (Date 31 12 2017) 601,
         `shekel period` (Date 1 1 2018)  (Date 31 5 2018)  712.62,
         `shekel period` (Date 1 6 2018)  (Date 30 11 2018) 843.11,
         `shekel period` (Date 1 12 2018) (Date 31 12 9999) 902.40

-- §2a: from 1.9.2017 these replace the amounts and dates of section 4 of
-- the agreement of 23.3.2017; §2b: that section's other rules (4c-4h),
-- among them any pro-rating for a part position, still govern the
-- supplement and are not encoded here.
@ref akn:art_2__para_a akn:art_2__para_b
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the updated shekel supplement for a full position on` `the day` IS
    sum (map (GIVEN p YIELD p's `full-position amount`)
             (filter (GIVEN p YIELD `the day` AT LEAST p's `period from` AND `the day` AT MOST p's `period to`)
                     `the updated shekel supplement 2016`))

-- The four periods follow one another without a gap or an overlap.
`the shekel periods are contiguous` MEANS
    all (GIVEN pair YIELD `Day` (pair's snd's `period from`) EQUALS `Day` (pair's fst's `period to`) PLUS 1)
        (zip (take 3 `the updated shekel supplement 2016`) (drop 1 `the updated shekel supplement 2016`))
#ASSERT `the shekel periods are contiguous`

§§ `3 שינוי שיעור תוספת דרגת קידום`

-- §3a: section 20(d) of the Oz LeTmura agreement, each promotion grade 2%
-- of the combined salary, becomes 1.69% from 1.9.2017 and 1.67% from
-- 1.12.2018.
@ref akn:art_3__para_a
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the rate of one promotion grade on` `the day` IS
    IF `the day` AT LEAST Date 1 12 2018
    THEN 0.0167
    ELSE IF `the day` AT LEAST Date 1 9 2017
         THEN 0.0169
         ELSE 0.02

@desc A printed row of the table that replaces section 20(11) of the Oz LeTmura agreement: the cumulative rate of the promotion grades, in percent.
DECLARE `promotion row` HAS
    `grades`                 IS A NUMBER
    `cumulative from 1.9.2017`  IS A NUMBER
    `cumulative from 1.12.2018` IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:art_3__para_b akn:art_3__para_b/p2 akn:art_3__para_b/t1
`the promotion-grade table` MEANS
    LIST `promotion row` 1 1.69 1.67,
         `promotion row` 2 3.38 3.35,
         `promotion row` 3 5.07 5.02,
         `promotion row` 4 6.76 6.69

-- The table's figures govern the supplement (it is the text that replaces
-- section 20(11)); see F-2017-18_tashach_01-b for how they square with §3a.
GIVEN `grades` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `cumulative promotion rate` `grades` `the day` IS
    sum (map (GIVEN r YIELD IF `the day` AT LEAST Date 1 12 2018
                            THEN r's `cumulative from 1.12.2018` DIVIDED BY 100
                            ELSE r's `cumulative from 1.9.2017` DIVIDED BY 100)
             (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `grades` EQUALS `grades`) `the promotion-grade table`))

-- akn:art_3__para_c The remaining rules on promotion grades (section 20 of Oz LeTmura as worded by the follow-up committee of 28.5.2013) are unchanged; a pointer, no rule of its own.

-- §3d: the new rate applies to existing teachers too.
@ref akn:art_3__para_d
GIVEN `already holds promotion grades` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the new promotion rate applies` `already holds promotion grades` IF TRUE

§§ `4 ביטול תוספות שכר`

@ref akn:art_4__para_a/p2 akn:art_4__para_a/p3 akn:art_4__para_a/p4 akn:art_4__para_a/p5 akn:art_4__para_a/p6 akn:art_4__para_a/p7 akn:art_4__para_a/p8
DECLARE `merged supplement` IS ONE OF
    `the 87 supplement`
    `the 94 supplement, teaching reinforcement`
    `the 2001 supplement`
    `the 2008 supplement`
    `the 2011 supplement`
    `the 2011 erosion supplement`
    `the 2016 percentage supplement`

-- §4a-§4b: from 1.9.2017 the merged supplements are no longer paid, nor
-- any right that flowed from paying them, whatever any agreement,
-- arrangement or practice says.
@ref akn:art_4__para_a akn:art_4__para_b
GIVEN s IS A `merged supplement`, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is paid on` s `the day` IF
    `the day` LESS THAN Date 1 9 2017

-- §4c: they are no longer a base for any other supplement.
@ref akn:art_4__para_c
GIVEN s IS A `merged supplement`, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a base for other supplements on` s `the day` IF
    `the day` LESS THAN Date 1 9 2017

-- §4c's example: the transition-to-reform supplement (section 24 of Oz
-- LeTmura) is computed from 1.9.2017 on the combined salary alone.
@ref akn:art_4__para_c akn:art_4__para_c/p2
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `combined salary` IS A NUMBER
      `the merged supplements` IS A NUMBER @desc the merged supplements the employee drew before 1.9.2017
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the base of the transition-to-reform supplement` `the day` `combined salary` `the merged supplements` IS
    IF `the day` AT LEAST Date 1 9 2017
    THEN `combined salary`
    ELSE `combined salary` PLUS `the merged supplements`

-- §4d: for the "87 transition-to-reform" supplement paid to principals, the
-- 87 supplement's shekel amount on the eve of the agreement is frozen as its
-- base (§4d(1)) and moves only by the mechanism of section 4(d) of the
-- agreement of 23.3.17 (§4d(2)), an input here.
@ref akn:art_4__para_d akn:art_4__para_d__subpara_1 akn:art_4__para_d__subpara_1/p2
`the frozen 87 amount` MEANS 177.05

@ref akn:art_4__para_d__subpara_2
GIVEN `update under section 4(d) of 23.3.17` IS A NUMBER @desc the cumulative update that mechanism gives, as a fraction; set elsewhere
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the amount the 87 transition supplement is computed on` `update under section 4(d) of 23.3.17` IS
    `the frozen 87 amount` TIMES (1 PLUS `update under section 4(d) of 23.3.17`)

§§ `5 ביצוע`

DECLARE `section of the agreement` IS ONE OF
    `section 1 tables`, `section 2 shekel supplement`, `section 3 promotion grades`, `section 4 merged supplements`

-- §5a-§5b: the four sections are one arrangement, carried out together and
-- at the same time or not at all.
@ref akn:art_5__para_a akn:art_5__para_b
GIVEN `sections implemented` IS A LIST OF `section of the agreement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the implementation is lawful` `sections implemented` IF
        count `sections implemented` EQUALS 0
    OR  all (GIVEN s YIELD elem s `sections implemented`)
            (LIST `section 1 tables`, `section 2 shekel supplement`, `section 3 promotion grades`, `section 4 merged supplements`)

DECLARE `implementation action` IS ONE OF
    `implement the agreement in the salary` HAS `arrears since 1.9.2017 paid` IS A NUMBER
    `deduct the overpayment` HAS `deducted` IS A NUMBER

-- §5c, in salary months from September 2017 (= 1): carried out from the
-- September salary and no later than the November salary (3); if later than
-- September, the differences since 1.9.2017 are paid in that month.
@ref akn:art_5__para_c
GIVEN `arrears owed` IS A NUMBER @desc the differences since 1.9.2017 at the month implementation begins
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `implementation action`
DECIDE `carrying out the agreement` `arrears owed` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `implement the agreement in the salary` `paid`
          PROVIDED `paid` AT LEAST `arrears owed`
    WITHIN 3
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 5c: no later than the salary for November 2017, with the differences since 1.9.2017"

-- §5d: up to the salary for January 2018 (salary month 5), an overpayment
-- made by an error in implementing the agreement counts as an advance on
-- wages under section 25(a)(7) of the Wage Protection Law 1958.
@ref akn:art_5__para_d akn:art_5__para_d/p2
GIVEN `salary month` IS A NUMBER @desc months from September 2017 (= 1)
      `overpaid by an error in implementing the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the overpayment counts as an advance on wages` `salary month` `overpaid by an error in implementing the agreement` IF
    `overpaid by an error in implementing the agreement` AND `salary month` AT MOST 5

-- §5e: written notice of the error 30 days before the deduction begins, and
-- a chance to respond. Time in days from the notice: no deduction for 30
-- days, then it may begin.
@ref akn:art_5__para_e
GIVEN `monthly instalment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `implementation action`
DECIDE `deducting an overpayment after notice` `monthly instalment` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    SHANT `deduct the overpayment` `any amount`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY `the employer`
           MAY `deduct the overpayment` `amount`
               PROVIDED `amount` AT MOST `monthly instalment`)
    LEST BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 5e: written notice 30 days before the deduction begins"

-- §5f: in twelve equal monthly parts.
@ref akn:art_5__para_f
GIVEN `overpayment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `monthly deduction of the overpayment` `overpayment` IS
    `overpayment` DIVIDED BY 12

-- akn:art_5__para_g The union's statement that the section admits no error in any salary; no rule.

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off and the copies list; no rule.

-- Findings.

-- F-2017-18_tashach_01-a: §3d and §4c cite the combined-salary update as
-- "section 3 above"; in this circular it is section 1, and section 3 is the
-- promotion-grade change.
`the section §3d and §4c cite for the table update` MEANS `section 3 promotion grades`
`the section that updates the tables` MEANS `section 1 tables`
`section 3 above is not the table update` MEANS
    NOT (`the section §3d and §4c cite for the table update` EQUALS `the section that updates the tables`)
#ASSERT `section 3 above is not the table update`

-- F-2017-18_tashach_01-b: from 1.12.2018 one grade is 1.67% (§3a), but the
-- table's cumulative rates for 2, 3 and 4 grades are not 2, 3 and 4 times it.
`the cumulative rates §3a gives from 1.12.2018` MEANS
    map (GIVEN n YIELD n TIMES 1.67) (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4)
`the cumulative rates the table prints from 1.12.2018` MEANS
    map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `cumulative from 1.12.2018`) `the promotion-grade table`
`the promotion table departs from the per-grade rate from 1.12.2018` MEANS
    `the cumulative rates §3a gives from 1.12.2018` EQUALS LIST 1.67, 3.34, 5.01, 6.68
    AND `the cumulative rates the table prints from 1.12.2018` EQUALS LIST 1.67, 3.35, 5.02, 6.69
#ASSERT `the promotion table departs from the per-grade rate from 1.12.2018`

-- From 1.9.2017 the table and §3a agree.
`the table agrees with section 3a from 1.9.2017` MEANS
    map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `cumulative from 1.9.2017`) `the promotion-grade table`
    EQUALS map (GIVEN n YIELD n TIMES 1.69) (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4)
#ASSERT `the table agrees with section 3a from 1.9.2017`

-- F-2017-18_tashach_01-c: the further 1.2% of 1.12.2018 applied to the
-- printed 1.9.2017 table, rounded to the agora, misses the printed
-- 1.12.2018 table by one agora in 36 of its 180 cells.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `to the agora` x IS TRUNC (x PLUS 0.005) 2

`all degrees` MEANS LIST `doctor`, `second degree`, `first degree`, `senior teacher`, `certified teacher`

GIVEN a IS A `salary row`, b IS A `salary row`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `cells that miss the 1.2% update` a b IS
    count (filter (GIVEN d YIELD NOT (`to the agora` (`the cell for` a d TIMES (1 PLUS `the further update of 1.12.2018`)) EQUALS `the cell for` b d))
                  `all degrees`)

`cells of the 1.12.2018 table that 1.2% on the 1.9.2017 table does not give` MEANS
    sum (zipWith `cells that miss the 1.2% update` `the combined-salary table from 1.9.2017` `the combined-salary table from 1.12.2018`)

`the 1.12.2018 table is not 1.2% on the printed 1.9.2017 table` MEANS
    `cells of the 1.12.2018 table that 1.2% on the 1.9.2017 table does not give` EQUALS 36
#ASSERT `the 1.12.2018 table is not 1.2% on the printed 1.9.2017 table`

-- None misses by more than an agora.
GIVEN a IS A `salary row`, b IS A `salary row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `every cell is within an agora` a b IF
    all (GIVEN d YIELD `the cell for` b d MINUS `the cell for` a d TIMES (1 PLUS `the further update of 1.12.2018`) AT MOST 0.01
                   AND `the cell for` a d TIMES (1 PLUS `the further update of 1.12.2018`) MINUS `the cell for` b d AT MOST 0.01)
        `all degrees`
#ASSERT and (zipWith `every cell is within an agora` `the combined-salary table from 1.9.2017` `the combined-salary table from 1.12.2018`)

-- Examples. Both tables have 36 rows, years 1 to 36.
#ASSERT map (GIVEN r YIELD r's `seniority year`) `the combined-salary table from 1.12.2018` EQUALS range 1 36
#ASSERT `combined salary` (Date 15 10 2017) `first degree` 10 0 EQUALS 4988.79
#ASSERT `combined salary` (Date 1 1 2019) `doctor` 36 0 EQUALS 8597.67
#ASSERT `the updated shekel supplement for a full position on` (Date 31 5 2018) EQUALS 712.62
#ASSERT `the updated shekel supplement for a full position on` (Date 1 12 2018) EQUALS 902.40
#ASSERT `cumulative promotion rate` 3 (Date 1 1 2018) EQUALS 0.0507
#ASSERT NOT `is paid on` `the 2008 supplement` (Date 1 9 2017)
#ASSERT `the implementation is lawful` (LIST `section 1 tables`, `section 2 shekel supplement`, `section 3 promotion grades`, `section 4 merged supplements`)
#ASSERT NOT `the implementation is lawful` (LIST `section 1 tables`, `section 2 shekel supplement`)
#ASSERT `monthly deduction of the overpayment` 1200 EQUALS 100

#TRACE `carrying out the agreement` 500 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `implement the agreement in the salary` 500 AT 3
#TRACE `carrying out the agreement` 500 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `implement the agreement in the salary` 500 AT 4
#TRACE `deducting an overpayment after notice` 100 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `deduct the overpayment` 100 AT 10
#TRACE `deducting an overpayment after notice` 100 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `deduct the overpayment` 100 AT 31
